HTTP Requests for EmailService
These examples demonstrate how to call your sendEmail action using .http format.

# 1. Basic Email (Plain Text Only)
# This request sends a simple email with only a plain text body.

### Send Basic Email (Plain Text) - with html body ...
POST http://localhost:4004/email/sendSmtpGmailEmail
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "krishnapk808@gmail.com",
  "subject": "CDSW Test EGmail: Plain Text Only",
  "body": "CDSW EGmail This is a test email sent from my CAP application handler, with only plain text content.",
  "htmlBody": "<p>CDSW EGmail This is a test email sent from my CAP application handler, with only plain text content.</p>"
}



# 2. Basic Email (HTML Body Only)
# This request sends an email with an HTML formatted body.

### Send Basic Email (HTML Body)
POST http://localhost:4004/email/sendSmtpGmailEmail
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "recipient@example.com",
  "subject": "Test Email: HTML Body",
  "htmlBody": "<h1>Hello from CAP!</h1><p>This is an <b>HTML</b> email sent from your Node.js CAP application.</p><p>It looks much nicer!</p>"
}

# 3. Basic Email (Both Plain Text and HTML Body)
# Nodemailer will prioritize the htmlBody if both are provided, but body serves as a fallback for email clients that don't support HTML.

### Send Basic Email (Plain Text and HTML)
POST http://localhost:4004/email/sendSmtpGmailEmail
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "recipient@example.com",
  "subject": "Test Email: Plain Text & HTML",
  "body": "This is the plain text fallback. If you see this, your email client doesn't support HTML.",
  "htmlBody": "<h2>Greetings!</h2><p>This email has <strong>both</strong> plain text and HTML versions. Your client should display this HTML.</p>"
}


# 4. Email with Single Attachment
# Before running: Create a file named test.txt in your srv directory (e.g., srv/test.txt) with some content.

### Send Email with Single Attachment
POST http://localhost:4004/email/sendSmtpGmailEmail
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "krishnapk808@gmail.com",
  "subject": "CDSGMW Test Email: With One Attachment",
  "body": "CDSW EGmail This is a test email sent from my CAP application handler, with only plain text content.",
  "htmlBody": "<p>CDSW EGmail This is a test email sent from my CAP application handler, with only plain text content.</p>",
  "attachments": [
    {
      "filename": "packagehehejson.txt",
      "path": "../srv/packagehehejson.txt",
      "contentType": "text/plain"
    }
  ]
}

# 5. Email with Multiple Attachments
# Before running: Create test.txt and image.png (or any other image file) in your srv directory.

### Send Email with Multiple Attachments
POST http://localhost:4004/email/sendSmtpGmailEmail
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "recipient@example.com",
  "subject": "Test Email: With Multiple Attachments",
  "htmlBody": "<p>Here are multiple files attached for your review:</p><ul><li>A text file</li><li>An image</li></ul>",
  "attachments": [
    {
      "filename": "important-notes.txt",
      "path": "./srv/test.txt",
      "contentType": "text/plain"
    },
    {
      "filename": "sample-image.png",
      "path": "./srv/image.png",
      "contentType": "image/png"
    }
  ]
}

# 6. Email to Multiple Recipients
# Separate multiple recipient email addresses with a comma.

### Send Email to Multiple Recipients
POST http://localhost:4004/email/sendSmtpGmailEmail
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "recipient1@example.com, recipient2@example.com",
  "subject": "Test Email: Multiple Recipients",
  "body": "This email is sent to multiple recipients at once."
}

# 7. Missing Required Parameters (Error Scenario)
# This request will trigger the validation error in your CAP service handler because subject is missing.

### Error Scenario: Missing Subject
POST http://localhost:4004/email/sendSmtpGmailEmail
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "recipient@example.com",
  "body": "This email should fail because the subject is missing."
}